    "chunk_size_bytes": 1077,
    "chunk_text": "India\u2013Sri Lanka Business Forum highlights new momentum in trade, investment and connectivity\n\nFrom left: Manish Mohan, Vishal Kamat, Anurag Agarwal, Dr. Rajesh Ravindra Gawande, Mahishini Colonne, Krishan Balendra, Duminda Hulangamuwa, Priyanga Wickramasinghe, and Shiran Fernando\n\nThe Ceylon Chamber of Commerce, in partnership with the Confederation of Indian Industry (CII), organised the India\u2013Sri Lanka Business Forum: Partnering in Sri Lanka\u2019s Growth and Investment and the CII \u2013 Ceylon Chamber CEOs Interaction in Mumbai on 13 May. The events brought together senior government representatives, industry leaders, policymakers, and business delegates from India and Sri Lanka to deepen economic engagement and explore new avenues for cooperation across priority sectors.\n\nThe discussions reflected growing optimism about India-Sri Lanka economic relations and focused on expanding collaboration in trade, investments, connectivity, tourism, renewable energy, logistics, digital transformation, infrastructure, healthcare, education, manufacturing, and technology."
