    "language": "en",
    "md5": "2a638751c17c152a7d38e6bf982504a6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1636,
    "chunk_text": "NCE Kurunegala visit \u2013 Meeting with aspiring exporters at EDB\n\nThe North Western Provincial Office of the Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB) successfully organised a networking meeting with the delegation of the National Chamber of Exporters of Sri Lanka (NCE) and potential exporters on 15 May 2026 in Kurunegala. The event was conducted as a parallel session to the B2B forum hosted by Industrial Services Bureau (ISB) \u2013 Kurunegala.\n\nThe primary objective of the meeting was to facilitate networking and collaboration opportunities between the NCE delegation and potential exporters, including export-ready entrepreneurs in the North Western Province (NWP). The programme also aimed to establish stronger supply chain linkages between leading exporters and local producers and suppliers within the province.\n\nThe event brought together members of the NCE delegation and aspiring exporters from the NWP, including start-ups and non-regular exporters, to discuss their export journeys, current market positions, and future business prospects. The session also provided an opportunity for participants to gain valuable knowledge and insights from established exporters, enabling them to strengthen and expand their export activities.\n\nThe meeting was attended by the NCE President Indhra Kaushal Rajapaksa, and the Secretary General/Chief Executive Officer Shiham Marikar accompanied by representatives of member organisations comprising established exporters and key service sector stakeholders, including logistics providers, financial institutions, insurance companies, certification bodies, and port terminal operators etc."
