    "chunk_size_bytes": 1877,
    "chunk_text": "Total Disarmament Only Panacea For Eternal World Peace\n\nThe recent Walk Mission for World Peace which commenced from Texas, USA, by a group of Buddhist Monks and reached our country, stirred me to write this essay. This Walk Mission, though spectacular, attracting world attention, is of no real value in achieving tangible World Peace. It serves as an advertisement for marketing religion. Even if its intent was to create awareness for world peace, it is superfluous, because the world is fully aware of the dire need for world peace. Walk Missions for Peace from one end of the world to other, cannot achieve World Peace. What is needed is concrete and productive action to achieve World Peace. Action to move World leaders of nations to take meaningful measures to secure world peace, both at national and international level, like the UNO, is the imperative need.\n\nTo achieve World Peace, the causes that generate wars, have to be eradicated, root and branch. World body of leaders, as a whole, has to take concrete measures to put an end to the ever-expanding militarization of the world. Peace and Armies are contradictory and cannot coexist. Voicing for world peace, whilst having standing Armies and Armories of destructive weapons, is a contradiction and counterproductive. If world needs Peace, Armies and Armories, have to be abolished, and if world needs Armies and Armories, Peace has to be sacrificed. Armies exist for the only reason to wage wars and no other. Then wars, either limited or unlimited, are inevitable.\n\nThere are two parallel and contradictory developments in the evolution of our human civilization:\n\na) World has reached the pinnacle in human civilization in all spheres of life: political, social, cultural, economic, science and technology, education, health and modern comforts and conveniences of living and great cities for people to live."
