    "md5": "2d745192e03b0f6eaade23b6b616b85b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 819,
    "chunk_text": "Children who are victims of abuse are entitled to dignity, privacy, and protection from further trauma. Public exposure, speculation, and sensational reporting risk causing additional harm to a child who has already endured enough. This must stop immediately.\n\nWe must also guard against attempts to politicise this matter or allow religious, political, racial, or social biases to influence the process.\n\nThis is a moment for institutions to act with clarity, courage, and professionalism.\n\nThe National Child Protection Authority, the Department of Probation and Child Care Services, Law Enforcement, and the Attorney-General\u2019s Department must take all necessary steps to ensure the child\u2019s protection and the integrity of the legal process.\n\nBut the child\u2019s welfare must remain at the centre of every decision."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
